@@ -147,3 +147,13 @@
 32 MiB aggregate client queue budget per server. Consumption releases byte
 reservations; queue exhaustion closes that client and releases its unsent tail.
 Normal stop still does not provide a final-event acknowledgement to clients.
+
+## Bundled OpenSSL payload ownership
+
+The OpenSSL decoder owns its payload bytes: compact events allocate only the
+validated data length; legacy fixed-layout events retain the 16 KiB wire body.
+Neither format borrows a perf-reader buffer, and Event.Clone copies payloads.
+The typed publisher still owns its envelope payload. eCaptureQ marshals
+synchronously, then transfers the fresh immutable wire buffer to its hub;
+generic hub.publish callers retain snapshot-copy semantics. These changes do
+not change protobuf fields or the compact kernel wire layout.
