--- a/docs/agent/probe-development.md
+++ b/docs/agent/probe-development.md
@@ -262,3 +262,9 @@
 The six previously reserved identity_pad bytes carry the low 48 bits of process
 start ticks; nonzero values prefix StreamID with PID:start_ticks/ without
 changing the compact record header size or legacy decoding.
+
+OpenSSL Event.Data is an owned byte slice rather than an inline maximum-sized
+array. When constructing synthetic events, provide the claimed bytes explicitly;
+Validate rejects a length beyond that slice. Compact decode copies exactly its
+validated length, and legacy decode still consumes the fixed 16 KiB body before
+its trailing header. Clone preserves independent payload ownership.
